 "notes": "Button prompt glyphs. Each prompt is a row: frame 0 = up, frame 1 = pressed (play the anim at 4 fps for a 'tap this' blink, or hold frame 1 while the button is held). Glyphs are left- and bottom-aligned in the cell; anchor = bottom-left; sizes[name] = [w, h] of the drawn glyph, for laying out text after it. Inline with font_small: put the glyph's bottom row on the text baseline + 2 (key caps are 11 px tall, the text caps 7 px) and leave 2 px on each side. pad_south/east/west/north are platform-neutral face-button positions (the lit dot is the button); pad_a/b/x/y are labelled Xbox-style. key_blank / key_blank_wide + font_tiny can make any other key."
